## How to Run on macOS Startup
To make the app run automatically every time you log into your Mac, choose one of the two methods below. Method 1 (Automator) is highly recommended for GUI applications.

## 1) Using Automator (Recommended & Easiest)
This method creates a small macOS app wrapper that you can easily add to your Login Items.

- Open the Automator app on your Mac.

- Click New Document and select Application.

- In the search bar on the left, type Run Shell Script and double-click it to add it to the workflow.

- Replace the default text in the script box with the following (make sure to replace /path/to/your/whisper_dictation with your actual absolute path):

Bash
#!/bin/bash
cd /path/to/your/whisper_dictation
./venv/bin/python main.py &
Press Cmd + S to save. Name it StartWhisper and save it to your Applications folder.

- Open System Settings -> General -> Login Items.

- Click the + button under "Open at Login" and select your new StartWhisper.app.
